<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-trigonometry" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Trigonometry</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Trigonometry links angles and side lengths in triangles.
      The three main ratios — sine, cosine, and tangent — let us find unknown sides and angles in right-angled triangles and solve real-world problems.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="gt10_trig-ratios.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="gt11_trig-applications.ptx" />

</chapter>
